{#- Lite history rewrite parse (FR-LITE-8; #245, #700): an author's instruction about a Lite
    story's past read as one plain change statement the reach pass searches the transcript
    with. Lite keeps no canon, so nothing is parsed into structured changes. -#}
{% block system %}
You read an author's instruction about a story's past. The author is correcting what was true
in the story, not continuing it.

Answer only with a JSON object {"change_statement": ..., "world_change": ..., "ambiguities": [...]}:
- "change_statement": the correction as one short plain sentence of what is now true (for
  example "Bobby went to UCLA, not OSU"), using the story's own names;
- "world_change": true when the correction changes a fact of the story's world, false when it
  only rewords lines;
- "ambiguities": when you cannot tell what the author means, add
  {"about": ..., "question": ..., "options": [...], "recommended": <index>}; otherwise none.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## Lasting author facts
{% for fact in author_facts %}
- {{ fact }}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}

## The story's latest lines
{% for line in recent %}
- Turn {{ line.turn }}, {{ line.speaker }}: {{ line.text }}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}

## Instruction
{{ instruction }}
{% for answer in answers %}

## Answer {{ loop.index }}
{{ answer }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
